WEBVTT

00:15.682 --> 00:18.393
When was the last time
we had the Sacred Banquet?

00:18.476 --> 00:21.271
Seeing that not just
the Senior First Rank Dragon Keepers

00:21.354 --> 00:23.982
but also the Junior First Ranks are here,

00:24.065 --> 00:26.776
are we going to have a change of members
after a long time?

00:27.110 --> 00:29.362
That aside,
why don't we eat first?

00:29.946 --> 00:32.032
I'm terribly hungry right now.

00:32.657 --> 00:34.367
That's the usual for you.

00:37.328 --> 00:38.955
The last person has arrived.

00:39.039 --> 00:40.874
Good, looks like we're all here.

00:40.957 --> 00:42.834
REWARD GOOD AND PUNISH EVIL

00:42.917 --> 00:44.169
Hey, Yellow.

00:44.252 --> 00:47.088
Looks like you didn't educate
your mistress well enough.

00:47.172 --> 00:48.882
She's late, and not even
an apology from her?

00:49.883 --> 00:51.634
My apologies.

00:51.718 --> 00:53.428
She always does things at her own pace.

00:54.137 --> 00:55.680
Say something, damn you!

00:56.264 --> 00:57.599
"Mistress"?

00:57.682 --> 01:00.060
The relationship between
Dragon Keepers and their buddies

01:00.143 --> 01:01.686
may vary in ways,

01:01.770 --> 01:05.315
but now I see how you view your own buddy.

01:05.899 --> 01:08.109
You act like some middle-school kid
who just entered puberty.

01:08.193 --> 01:09.194
The hell did you say?

01:09.277 --> 01:10.278
You jerk!

01:10.361 --> 01:11.446
Stop!

01:11.863 --> 01:13.073
Ouch...

01:13.448 --> 01:15.492
The hell are you doing, Aizome?

01:15.575 --> 01:18.161
Blue. The way you speak
and act is really horrible,

01:18.244 --> 01:20.580
so you have to be a taciturn character
like we talked about!

01:20.663 --> 01:23.041
You stay back!
Stop this, you fools!

01:25.085 --> 01:27.337
What are you doing,
fighting with your own comrades?

01:28.171 --> 01:30.215
You freaking idiot,
why are you acting so high and mighty?

01:30.298 --> 01:34.094
- Mind your own business! You little...
- My lovable body is going to break!

01:34.177 --> 01:36.221
Let's just leave it at that, shall we?

01:38.807 --> 01:41.059
Farewell!

01:43.144 --> 01:44.813
You, Yellow Junior First Rank.

01:45.522 --> 01:48.233
What should you do
if you've done something wrong?

01:52.612 --> 01:56.533
Everyone, I'm deeply sorry
to have kept you waiting.

01:56.616 --> 01:59.702
Good! Now we can get down to business.

01:59.786 --> 02:01.121
Hear me out while you guys eat.

02:04.040 --> 02:05.041
I messed up.

02:05.125 --> 02:06.292
- Huh?
- What?

02:06.376 --> 02:09.087
I think my Divine Artifact was stolen!

02:14.467 --> 02:16.427
Go! Go! Loser Ranger!

03:40.511 --> 03:42.263
If you got your Divine Artifact stolen...

03:42.764 --> 03:44.057
Isn't that really bad?

03:44.140 --> 03:45.934
Don't eat my food!

03:46.017 --> 03:48.728
R-Red! Is that true?

03:48.811 --> 03:52.440
Yeah. It's probably taken
by the fighter I killed this morning.

03:53.066 --> 03:54.567
<i>Thanks to him, I can't transform.</i>

03:54.651 --> 03:56.361
<i>I'm even wearing
the outfit for the attraction show.</i>

03:57.153 --> 03:59.155
I don't like wearing this
since it gets stuffy.

03:59.239 --> 04:01.574
A mere fighter managed to do that?

04:01.658 --> 04:03.159
I can't believe this...

04:03.243 --> 04:04.869
It's been 12 years already.

04:04.953 --> 04:08.331
It completely slipped my mind that
there's a chance they could betray us.

04:08.414 --> 04:13.670
However, if that fighter
didn't possess the Divine Artifact...

04:13.753 --> 04:15.588
Could he have hidden it somewhere?

04:16.005 --> 04:17.006
Or perhaps,

04:17.799 --> 04:20.969
there's a possibility
that he has given it to someone else.

04:22.303 --> 04:25.348
An utterly unforgivable act.

04:26.099 --> 04:28.643
I shall bring down
the hammer of justice upon him!

04:29.227 --> 04:30.812
There's not many who are
aware of the deal we made

04:30.895 --> 04:32.063
with the monsters.

04:32.146 --> 04:34.816
As a way to get our act together
once again,

04:34.899 --> 04:37.568
let's come up with countermeasures--
One moment, please.

04:38.861 --> 04:40.655
Yes, countermeasures must be taken.

04:41.114 --> 04:42.865
But aside from that...

04:42.949 --> 04:46.536
I believe you should take responsibility
for this major blunder.

04:46.619 --> 04:49.080
You've committed a big mistake, Red.

04:49.163 --> 04:51.291
And you still intend
to remain as a Senior First Rank?

04:51.374 --> 04:52.875
Cut it! We're in a state of emergency--

04:52.959 --> 04:55.086
And who's the one
who caused this emergency?

04:55.503 --> 04:57.672
<i>The Divine Artifact is the cornerstone
of the Rangers!</i>

04:57.755 --> 05:00.425
<i>The last hope that protects humans
from monsters!</i>

05:00.508 --> 05:03.052
<i>It's outrageous that it's been stolen!</i>

05:03.136 --> 05:06.306
You should resign from your position
as the Dragon Keeper!

05:06.389 --> 05:08.016
<i>So much for all that talk,</i>

05:08.391 --> 05:11.394
<i>when you're the one who leaked
the information on the Divine Artifact.</i>

05:12.270 --> 05:15.315
<i>Man, do I hate the adult world.</i>

05:16.607 --> 05:17.608
You're right.

05:18.401 --> 05:19.777
It's just as you said.

05:20.278 --> 05:21.946
I should resign as the Red Keeper.

05:22.030 --> 05:23.531
Huh?

05:24.157 --> 05:27.368
I know better than anyone
that you've been working really hard.

05:28.161 --> 05:30.371
There's no rule saying
we should appoint in order of rank,

05:30.455 --> 05:32.540
but I'll be glad to hand
the position to you.

05:32.623 --> 05:33.666
Of course!

05:33.750 --> 05:36.294
Ever since I saw Red Keeper in action
when I was a kid,

05:36.502 --> 05:39.422
I've worked my way up here
with only that one goal in mind!

05:39.505 --> 05:40.882
I can do it!

05:41.215 --> 05:44.260
I'll protect peace
in a way that's different from yours!

05:45.386 --> 05:47.221
In justice lies strength.

05:55.021 --> 05:57.523
R-Red...

05:58.024 --> 06:00.443
What's this? It doesn't look like
you're stronger than me.

06:00.943 --> 06:02.195
Then it won't do!

06:02.779 --> 06:03.946
You disappoint me!

06:04.030 --> 06:05.198
Akabane! Stop!

06:08.284 --> 06:10.661
<i>Right, my story was interrupted.</i>

06:11.162 --> 06:14.082
Well then, I don't mind
if you guys listen while we eat.

06:14.665 --> 06:15.666
Shall we continue?

06:18.294 --> 06:19.295
Delicious!

06:19.670 --> 06:21.798
<i>So much for being the allies of justice.</i>

06:23.132 --> 06:24.384
I don't like this.

06:24.467 --> 06:27.512
I agree. I've lost my appetite.

06:27.595 --> 06:29.055
- Not that.
- Huh?

06:30.306 --> 06:31.849
Something bothers me.

06:39.774 --> 06:42.610
I'll gamble on... this explosion.

06:45.238 --> 06:48.324
Listen up, Hekiru.
This would be the worst-case scenario.

06:49.117 --> 06:53.204
<i>That fighter manages to get away alive
and escapes with Red's Divine Artifact.</i>

06:53.996 --> 06:56.207
The fighter has two choices.

06:56.958 --> 06:59.210
<i>Either he gets drawn
into the floating fortress,</i>

06:59.293 --> 07:01.337
<i>or he gets swept away by the wind.</i>

07:02.088 --> 07:03.506
I'll search the fortress.

07:03.923 --> 07:06.050
You calculate the wind direction
and trace his location.

07:15.810 --> 07:16.811
<i>I'm alive.</i>

07:17.728 --> 07:20.731
<i>Suzukiri's explosives saved me again.</i>

07:21.441 --> 07:23.276
Argh, damn it!

07:23.359 --> 07:25.528
The hole on my stomach won't close up!

07:25.611 --> 07:27.363
So this is the power
of the Divine Artifact...

07:28.114 --> 07:29.115
<i>However...</i>

07:29.824 --> 07:31.451
<i>I haven't lost yet...</i>

07:32.326 --> 07:34.454
<i>Too bad that we're immortal.</i>

07:35.329 --> 07:37.790
<i>You'll remember this, you damn Rangers...</i>

07:38.458 --> 07:40.042
<i>I'll put an end to you guys.</i>

07:40.585 --> 07:42.962
<i>I'll... achieve...</i>

07:43.629 --> 07:45.715
<i>world domination!</i>

07:50.595 --> 07:52.889
I knew it. You survived.

07:55.516 --> 07:57.685
You... Why are you here?

07:57.768 --> 07:59.145
"Why", you ask?

07:59.228 --> 08:02.273
There's only one thing
a Ranger wants from a monster.

08:02.940 --> 08:04.901
Since you can't die no matter what,

08:05.401 --> 08:07.987
- I'm here to assist you.
- Assist?

08:08.070 --> 08:09.780
I'm a damn monster!

08:09.864 --> 08:12.533
You're so hot-headed!

08:14.076 --> 08:16.412
Damn it...

08:16.913 --> 08:19.874
I can't move properly
because of my stomach injury...

08:20.374 --> 08:22.752
I don't know if it'll work on your injury,

08:22.835 --> 08:25.171
but I brought along some stuff
for first-aid treatment.

08:25.254 --> 08:26.964
Eh?

08:27.048 --> 08:28.424
1. Beheading one to reduce
one's pain 2. Caring for someone

08:28.508 --> 08:30.384
That's what you meant by "assist"?

08:31.260 --> 08:32.595
Hey!

08:32.678 --> 08:34.138
Stop it!

08:34.222 --> 08:37.517
I haven't fallen so low that I'd need
someone from the Rangers to care for me!

08:38.059 --> 08:40.019
- Ouch... That hurt.
- Is that so?

08:40.520 --> 08:44.190
In that case, can't you close your wound
with your ability as a monster?

08:44.273 --> 08:47.318
I mean, if you can change your face,
then surely your wound...

08:47.401 --> 08:48.945
There's no way I can do that...

08:49.654 --> 08:52.448
- So I guess you can't do it!
- What? I sure as hell can!

08:52.532 --> 08:54.158
Oh, right...

08:54.617 --> 08:57.328
If I just transfer
a part of my arm to my stomach...

09:01.207 --> 09:02.708
Wow!

09:02.792 --> 09:04.794
Don't stare at my delicate parts!

09:04.877 --> 09:06.128
Oh, I'm sorry!

09:06.212 --> 09:08.589
It was rather impolite of me,
but I just couldn't look away!

09:08.673 --> 09:10.466
This is a power
beyond human understanding!

09:10.550 --> 09:13.594
A miracle indeed!
How great! How wonderful!

09:16.514 --> 09:18.307
This much is nothing.

09:18.391 --> 09:20.184
Wow! Bravo!

09:20.268 --> 09:22.478
This ain't a show, you know?

09:23.020 --> 09:24.438
Do you have any requests?

09:24.522 --> 09:26.148
Please change into my face!

09:26.732 --> 09:27.984
Oh.

09:28.067 --> 09:29.819
- I'm Hibiki.
- It's a miracle!

09:30.319 --> 09:32.446
Are you able to make
your face into a mask?

09:32.530 --> 09:33.531
Easy-peasy.

09:35.032 --> 09:37.159
- Amazing!
- Here you go.

09:39.954 --> 09:42.707
Look! Now I'm a fighter too!

09:44.166 --> 09:46.836
Are you dumb?
You ain't good enough to be one of us!

09:46.919 --> 09:49.672
Can you stand the fear
of being blown up every time?

09:49.755 --> 09:52.550
I-I don't think I can.

09:54.010 --> 09:55.803
My stomach still hurts.

09:55.886 --> 09:57.555
Is that all you need from me?

09:57.638 --> 09:59.390
I want to learn about you.

10:00.141 --> 10:02.059
I want you to learn about me, too.

10:02.476 --> 10:03.561
I refuse.

10:05.521 --> 10:07.565
- Ever since I was a kid...
- Hey, are you listening?

10:07.648 --> 10:10.568
- I've always wanted to do the right thing.
- Oh, so you're just going to continue?

10:13.821 --> 10:14.822
Hey!

10:16.782 --> 10:18.743
I'm glad you're fine.

10:18.826 --> 10:20.745
That's not right, Hibiki.

10:20.828 --> 10:21.996
Ah...

10:22.455 --> 10:24.915
Even crows must eat, or they'll die.

10:25.333 --> 10:28.419
All lives are equally precious.

10:28.502 --> 10:34.675
It would be presumptuous for us humans
to tip the scales of life intentionally.

10:38.679 --> 10:40.431
<i>My justice is my parents,</i>

10:41.098 --> 10:42.850
<i>and that was everything to me.</i>

10:45.853 --> 10:47.855
<i>Breaking news.
A mysterious flying object</i>

10:47.938 --> 10:50.024
<i>has been detected
above the skies of Amanogawa city.</i>

10:50.107 --> 10:53.319
<i>All residents in the vicinity
are to evacuate immediately.</i>

10:56.113 --> 10:57.782
Are we going to die?

10:58.115 --> 11:00.868
Everything is God's gift to us.

11:01.369 --> 11:02.745
The same goes for that UFO.

11:03.329 --> 11:06.791
It's possible that it came here
to correct the ways of humans

11:06.874 --> 11:08.709
who are destroying Earth
due to their greed.

11:08.793 --> 11:10.503
In that case, there's no need to worry.

11:10.586 --> 11:14.215
God will never abandon us
since we've been living a righteous life.

11:14.298 --> 11:16.217
Yeah, you're right.
Yes.

11:16.801 --> 11:20.221
Why are you following me? You're getting
in the way of my night practice.

11:20.763 --> 11:23.224
I've got to make sure
you don't draw bad guys to you

11:23.307 --> 11:24.934
since you're pretty, Big Sister.

11:25.017 --> 11:28.646
I'm not so weak that I'd need
a small child like you to protect me.

11:28.729 --> 11:29.855
What?

11:29.939 --> 11:31.982
You're too fast, Big Sister!

11:32.566 --> 11:34.777
No matter what you say,
I'll protect those precious to me!

11:34.860 --> 11:36.946
No matter how strong the enemy may be!

11:39.323 --> 11:41.701
- Big Sister...
- That was Red Keeper's line.

11:42.868 --> 11:44.787
We're not allowed to watch that, remember?

11:44.870 --> 11:47.289
Dad says we can't watch it
since it's violent.

11:47.373 --> 11:48.874
But he's so cool!

11:48.958 --> 11:50.501
I want to be like him, too!

11:50.584 --> 11:52.753
I'm surprised to hear that from you
since you always listen to our parents.

11:52.837 --> 11:54.255
Huh? What do you mean?

11:54.338 --> 11:58.592
If you like the Dragon Keepers,
does that mean Dad's wrong?

11:58.676 --> 12:00.720
That's not it...

12:00.803 --> 12:02.888
Then, is Dad right?

12:02.972 --> 12:05.099
What? Isn't that a given?

12:05.766 --> 12:08.102
Guess it's too hard
for a small child like you to understand.

12:10.688 --> 12:15.025
<i>Still, I've never thought
that my parents could be wrong.</i>

12:15.693 --> 12:17.194
They're amazing!

12:17.278 --> 12:18.529
The allies of justice!

12:21.073 --> 12:22.783
What a bunch of savages.

12:22.867 --> 12:25.327
The only reason the monsters
are using force is because

12:25.411 --> 12:29.540
you guys are all armed up
and trying to solve this with violence!

12:29.623 --> 12:31.876
And no one even realizes that...

12:31.959 --> 12:35.129
Right? What a horrifying world
we live in, Hibiki!

12:36.422 --> 12:38.549
<i>There's no way Dad and Mom could be wrong...</i>

12:39.467 --> 12:41.218
<i>I'm the one that's wrong.</i>

12:44.513 --> 12:45.556
<i>And one day,</i>

12:46.348 --> 12:47.641
<i>God descended.</i>

12:50.436 --> 12:54.774
Everyone. The day that our assembly
bears fruition is finally here!

12:54.857 --> 12:56.692
Our prayers shall be answered,

12:56.776 --> 12:59.195
- and everyone will achieve salvation!
- Thank goodness...

12:59.278 --> 13:01.822
God has descended upon us.

13:02.281 --> 13:03.866
Hibiki, you can't go!

13:03.949 --> 13:05.743
Why are you stopping me?

13:07.620 --> 13:10.831
Why am I stopping you?
Why don't you think for yourself?

13:10.915 --> 13:11.957
Huh.

13:24.094 --> 13:27.014
Hello, I'm God.

13:27.097 --> 13:29.517
Are you my believers too?

13:30.017 --> 13:32.645
In that case, I'll save you guys.

13:35.105 --> 13:36.941
Dad? Mom?

13:37.024 --> 13:38.025
Hibiki!

13:45.115 --> 13:46.867
Hibiki! Hibiki!

13:47.368 --> 13:49.286
Hibiki! Are you okay?

13:49.370 --> 13:50.871
Y-Yeah...

13:50.955 --> 13:53.165
I'm so glad... that you're safe...

13:57.253 --> 13:58.379
Big Sister!

13:58.462 --> 14:00.881
I'm sorry that I caused you pain.

14:00.965 --> 14:03.092
I'll end this quickly.

14:03.968 --> 14:05.427
<i>What's going on?</i>

14:05.511 --> 14:07.680
<i>If all lives are equal,</i>

14:08.055 --> 14:09.890
<i>does this mean there's nothing I can do</i>

14:10.724 --> 14:14.144
<i>about Dad and Mom's deaths,
as well as Big Sister dying?</i>

14:14.228 --> 14:16.146
Run, Hibiki!

14:17.231 --> 14:18.899
I'll protect those precious to me!

14:19.608 --> 14:21.944
No matter how strong the enemy may be!

14:23.863 --> 14:25.781
<i>Somehow, I managed to survive</i>

14:26.282 --> 14:29.159
<i>and made my decision
to join the Rangers and fight.</i>

14:31.245 --> 14:33.747
However, there was no hope there.

14:38.043 --> 14:39.962
Too long! That was too freaking long!

14:40.045 --> 14:42.423
If I weren't hurt,
I would've just kicked you aside and left!

14:42.506 --> 14:43.757
Sorry!

14:44.508 --> 14:46.176
Um... What's your name?

14:46.760 --> 14:48.679
You used a fake name for the exam, right?

14:48.762 --> 14:50.431
As if I'm telling you.

14:50.806 --> 14:52.600
If you want to run, now's the chance.

14:52.683 --> 14:54.977
I won against that panda dude, you know.

14:55.060 --> 14:57.730
Against Shun?
Isn't he a Senior Third Rank?

14:57.813 --> 15:00.065
I think he mentioned that.
What's that anyway?

15:00.858 --> 15:03.277
You won against the fifth-strongest member

15:03.360 --> 15:04.987
of the Red Squadron. Huh?

15:05.571 --> 15:07.656
You're grinning so much.

15:08.449 --> 15:11.827
I see... The fifth-strongest, huh?

15:11.911 --> 15:13.495
The rank's a little low, though.

15:13.579 --> 15:15.247
I've underestimated you.

15:15.331 --> 15:17.666
Indeed. I'm a true weapon of war.

15:17.750 --> 15:19.168
The threat to humanity!

15:19.251 --> 15:21.253
That's right!
I'm a strong, mighty warrior!

15:21.337 --> 15:23.005
In that case, the one
to defeat the Rangers...

15:23.088 --> 15:25.883
Of course it'll be me,
the mighty Fighter D!

15:25.966 --> 15:28.218
-"Fighter D"...
- Oops.

15:28.761 --> 15:30.387
How dare you trick me!

15:30.471 --> 15:32.056
I'm sorry!

15:32.139 --> 15:35.935
But if it means that people will stop
grieving over this meaningless war,

15:36.018 --> 15:37.478
I'll do anything!

15:39.355 --> 15:42.399
So D, I have a favor to ask.

15:47.988 --> 15:50.699
C-Come out if you're around, Fighter...

15:51.617 --> 15:54.078
I don't want to be covered
with all these leaves already...

15:56.580 --> 15:57.873
Junior Third Rank Hekiru!

15:58.457 --> 16:01.001
I'm Hibiki Sakurama,
an Independent Ranger!

16:01.085 --> 16:03.003
I-It's reassuring to see a comrade here.

16:03.587 --> 16:06.507
Did you... see a monster around here?

16:07.466 --> 16:10.511
Yes. I've managed
to capture an injured fighter.

16:11.595 --> 16:12.680
This way.

16:14.932 --> 16:17.017
Did he... save me?

16:19.436 --> 16:21.021
A-Are we there yet?

16:21.605 --> 16:24.525
I took the wrong route.
This is strange.

16:25.025 --> 16:26.443
Are we there yet?

16:26.527 --> 16:27.653
Just a little longer.

16:27.736 --> 16:28.821
It's just up ahead.

16:32.282 --> 16:34.952
M-Make sure you don't make
a mistake next time.

16:35.411 --> 16:36.412
I won't.

16:36.495 --> 16:38.080
I found the monster!

16:38.956 --> 16:40.332
What? Where?

16:41.041 --> 16:42.042
Over here.

16:44.628 --> 16:46.422
Don't look down on me, hoodie dude.

16:46.505 --> 16:49.425
Your restraints were so clumsy
that I broke out of it easily.

16:49.508 --> 16:52.970
- You with bangs! Junior Third Rank, huh?
- <i>Why go to all the trouble to do this?</i>

16:53.053 --> 16:55.055
Is that higher
than a Senior Third Rank?

16:55.139 --> 16:57.766
N-No... I'm one rank lower than that.

16:58.225 --> 17:00.769
Oh, really?
This'll be a piece of cake, then!

17:00.853 --> 17:03.272
<i>D... Are you trying to help me?</i>

17:03.355 --> 17:05.024
The hell are you staring at, hoodie dude?

17:05.357 --> 17:08.277
How about you three stop getting cold feet
and come at me all at once?

17:08.819 --> 17:10.654
Huh? What do you mean by "three"?

17:10.738 --> 17:12.573
What?
Isn't that dude with you guys?

17:18.620 --> 17:21.331
That... hurts!

17:21.415 --> 17:24.293
How mean! You're so mean! You hit me!

17:24.376 --> 17:26.837
<i>I was trying to split him in two. Damn it!</i>

17:27.379 --> 17:29.298
<i>My body is getting brittle!</i>

17:29.381 --> 17:31.717
How dare you trick me!

17:31.800 --> 17:36.805
You probably took down Red's Senior
Third Rank with a similar dirty trick!

17:36.889 --> 17:38.432
Divine Artifact, Manifest!

17:40.267 --> 17:42.311
Blue Dragon Leviathan!

17:44.897 --> 17:48.192
Huh? Aren't Divine Artifacts
exclusive to Dragon Keepers only?

17:48.776 --> 17:50.652
This is just a replica.

17:50.736 --> 17:54.406
However, it is capable
of destroying your kind!

17:55.908 --> 17:56.909
D!

17:57.409 --> 17:59.578
<i>I didn't hear about this, Suzukiri!</i>

17:59.661 --> 18:01.163
<i>The hell is this replica thing?</i>

18:08.045 --> 18:09.338
Huh?

18:12.966 --> 18:15.469
<i>What the heck's
with that Divine Artifact knockoff?</i>

18:15.552 --> 18:17.638
<i>You should've told me
about this, Suzukiri!</i>

18:21.016 --> 18:22.935
<i>No, I can't rely on others.</i>

18:23.018 --> 18:24.937
<i>I have to overcome this alone!</i>

18:25.104 --> 18:28.315
<i>Otherwise, I'll never make it
to the Dragon Keepers!</i>

18:29.358 --> 18:32.319
<i>D... You really plan to fight.</i>

18:33.362 --> 18:35.280
<i>Until all your enemies are taken down.</i>

18:39.493 --> 18:42.579
J-J-Just how long do you intend on hiding?

18:45.040 --> 18:48.085
Don't ignore me!

18:55.592 --> 18:57.136
Huh? Wait...

18:58.387 --> 19:00.514
No... Did he get away?

19:00.597 --> 19:02.099
Don't flatter yourself.

19:02.432 --> 19:03.892
If this is a game of hide-and-seek...

19:04.601 --> 19:06.770
I'm... it!

19:08.856 --> 19:12.484
Gotcha!

19:12.568 --> 19:14.486
No matter how powerful
a projectile weapon can be,

19:14.570 --> 19:16.572
it's useless once I get into close range!

19:16.655 --> 19:18.699
I win!

19:19.408 --> 19:20.450
Huh?

19:20.534 --> 19:23.328
Ouch... O-O-Ouch! It burns!

19:25.539 --> 19:26.832
The hell's wrong with that thing?

19:27.166 --> 19:28.375
It's melting!

19:30.878 --> 19:34.339
That's the power I borrowed from Blue.

19:34.423 --> 19:38.927
Th-The power of bonds is the reason
why I'm able to fight like this.

19:39.011 --> 19:40.929
Huh?
What are you talking about?

19:41.013 --> 19:42.848
You probably don't understand.

19:43.432 --> 19:46.018
<i>I have a leader I respect,</i>

19:46.101 --> 19:48.061
<i>colleagues... that I can trust,</i>

19:48.145 --> 19:52.357
<i>reliable juniors...
a-and people that I have to protect!</i>

19:53.275 --> 19:56.820
The power of bonds makes humans strong!

19:56.904 --> 19:57.905
Uh?

19:58.197 --> 19:59.573
Stupid!

20:02.534 --> 20:03.660
You...

20:05.245 --> 20:07.748
I-I'm so sorry, Hekiru!

20:08.165 --> 20:12.169
<i>They might have switched
identities with the monster's ability.</i>

20:12.252 --> 20:14.546
Y-You keep playing dirty until the end...

20:14.630 --> 20:16.298
You've got to hand over
the Replica Divine Artifact

20:16.381 --> 20:17.382
to the monster!

20:17.466 --> 20:19.801
Otherwise, I'm going to die!

20:19.885 --> 20:21.929
<i>If only I knew
whether they're colluding,</i>

20:22.012 --> 20:25.557
<i>or if they've switched identities,
I'd be able to take the initiative!</i>

20:25.641 --> 20:26.934
<i>I'll find that out now!</i>

20:27.017 --> 20:29.061
I-I got it...

20:29.519 --> 20:30.520
Sakurama.

20:31.021 --> 20:33.398
Y-You were a fine Ranger.

20:33.482 --> 20:34.483
Don't tell me...

20:38.487 --> 20:41.448
I've requested assistance
from the HQ just now!

20:41.531 --> 20:44.409
So it's just for a while!
Please hold on just for a little longer!

20:44.493 --> 20:46.328
<i>If they know
I sacrificed a Ranger</i>

20:46.411 --> 20:49.873
<i>just to deal with a fighter,
it'll be really bad!</i>

20:51.166 --> 20:52.584
There's no choice.

20:52.668 --> 20:53.877
I'll listen to you.

20:55.379 --> 20:58.298
Get back!
Leave the Divine Artifact!

21:11.061 --> 21:14.690
As if I'll hand it over
to the likes of you monster!

21:20.737 --> 21:22.197
<i>That's the real one!</i>

21:22.281 --> 21:24.032
They didn't switch!

21:24.116 --> 21:26.410
H-How dare you hurt me!

21:28.370 --> 21:30.289
I-It's dangerous!

21:41.383 --> 21:42.718
D-Did you get him?

21:43.510 --> 21:45.554
I apologize for acting
at my own discretion.

21:45.929 --> 21:47.806
I just couldn't forgive him.

21:48.390 --> 21:51.268
However, I couldn't have done
anything on my own.

21:51.768 --> 21:55.647
This is only possible because you lent me
this special power of yours.

21:56.273 --> 21:59.151
Um... So how should I say this?

22:00.235 --> 22:01.778
This is the power of our bond, I guess?

22:01.862 --> 22:02.863
Huh?

22:13.999 --> 22:15.417
It went well.

22:16.168 --> 22:18.545
But still, it really hurts.

22:28.180 --> 22:30.223
Are you really sure about this?

22:31.058 --> 22:34.394
There's no way you can win if you take
the Replica Divine Artifact head-on.

22:34.895 --> 22:36.480
- So...
- Huh?

22:36.563 --> 22:38.148
Huh?

22:38.231 --> 22:40.233
Huh? W-W-Wait!
What the hell are you doing?

22:40.317 --> 22:42.361
Your arm's not going
to grow back, you know?

22:42.444 --> 22:44.988
Compared to the injuries
you've suffered all this time,

22:45.072 --> 22:47.032
this is nothing but a scratch.

22:47.115 --> 22:48.992
Just how much of a nutjob can you be?

22:50.369 --> 22:55.874
D. If you really want to win, then please
go with my plan and don't fight him.

22:56.458 --> 23:00.170
Live as me, and find the answers
you couldn't find before.

23:00.253 --> 23:01.797
- I can't do that.
- What?

23:03.173 --> 23:05.425
I thought I'd already taken
a drastic enough measure...

23:05.842 --> 23:07.719
I'm a monster, and you're a Ranger.

23:08.428 --> 23:10.013
Fighting is the only thing we can do.

23:10.931 --> 23:12.808
So let's have a match.

23:15.310 --> 23:17.729
I'll crush the Ranger Force first.

23:17.813 --> 23:19.314
I won't let you have your way.

23:19.940 --> 23:22.359
I'll fix the Ranger Force first.

23:29.908 --> 23:31.910
Translated by Qianni Lu

23:32.411 --> 23:33.954
- Hi. Welcome!
- Fighter-kun?

23:34.037 --> 23:35.372
Wait, is this some kind
of sushi restaurant?

23:35.455 --> 23:37.833
- Hi. Welcome!
- I'll have the chef's recommendation then!

23:37.916 --> 23:39.918
Oh, thank you!

23:40.001 --> 23:42.838
One serving of the next episode,
"Fighter D, as a Part of 'Ranger Force'"!

23:42.921 --> 23:45.632
- Wait, where did he pop out from?
- Hi. Welcome!

23:45.715 --> 23:46.925
- Hi. Welcome!
- Munch.
